# Setup:
# 1. Install REST Client extension for VS Code.
# 2. Cmd > Preferences: Open User Settings (JSON)
# 3. Add:
#   "rest-client.environmentVariables": {
#     "$shared": {
#         "exnotaJwt": "<jwt>", # get from auth/login
#         "notionAccessToken": "<token>",
#         "notionOauthClientId": "<client_id>",
#         "notionBotId": "<bot_id>",
#         "notionWorkspaceId": "<workspace_id>",
#         "notionOwnerUserId": "<owner.id>",
#         "openAiKey": "<key>"
#     },
#     "local": {
#         "baseUrl": "http://localhost:3000"
#     },
#     "production": {
#         "baseUrl": "https://exnota.com/api"
#     }
#   }
# 4. Follow two 'Notion setup' steps below to get the data needed for "$shared"
#    environment variables and use then instead of the placeholders above.
#
# Usage:
# 1. Change environment:
#      * Cmd (⇧⌘P) > Rest Client: Switch Environment
#      * This will fix red lines.
# 2. Quick navigation
#      * Search (⌘P) > '@'

### ----------------------------------------------------
### note endpoints
### ----------------------------------------------------
### get notes
GET {{baseUrl}}/note/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{exnotaJwt}}

### post notes - m4a short
POST {{baseUrl}}/note/notes
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="type"
Content-Type: application/json

audio
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="notionInfo"
Content-Type: application/json

{"accessToken":"{{notionAccessToken}}","botId":"{{notionBotId}}","workspaceId":"{{notionWorkspaceId}}","ownerUserId":"{{notionOwnerUserId}}"}
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="short-test.m4a"
Content-Type: audio/x-m4a

< short-test.m4a
--boundary--

